## Answer

**Performance Metric Threshold:** 38% recall on technical queries (below the 40% SLA minimum)

**Enterprise Client:** DataCorp

**Context:** DataCorp had a 500GB technical documentation corpus where their engineering team couldn't find specific API method names using the BM25 sparse search algorithm. Bob's diagnostics on 2024-10-05 revealed the 38% recall rate, which alice confirmed on 2024-10-07 was unacceptable and below their 40% SLA minimum. This specific failure at DataCorp was the catalyst that forced the team to abandon pure sparse search and begin investigating dense embedding alternatives.

